<title>EGYPT: Egypt says buys 200,000T Argentine wheat.</title>
<headline>Egypt says buys 200,000T Argentine wheat.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-12-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt said on Sunday it bought 200,000 tonne of Argentine wheat at prices ranging from $130-132 per tonne FOB.</p>
<p>Samir Shakankiri, vice chairman of the General Authority for Supply Commodities, told Reuters he bought the wheat in four separate batches.</p>
<p>-- 50,000 tonnes at $130.97 for loading January 1997.</p>
<p>-- 50,000 tonnes at $131.95 for loading Jan 10-31 1997.</p>
<p>-- 50,000 tonnes at $132 for loading Feb 10-28 1997.</p>
<p>-- 50,000 tonnes at $132 for loading Feb 16-18 1997.</p>
<p>Shakankiri said he did not buy U.S. or French wheat because their prices were not competitive.</p>
<p>-- Mona Eltahawy, Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
